DELETE /2.0/folders/{folder_id}/metadata/{scope}/{template_key}
Deletes a piece of folder metadata.
Required: folder_id (path) — The unique identifier that represent a folder. The ID for any folder can be determined by visiting this folder in the web application and copying the ID from the URL. For example, for the URL `https://*.app.box.com/folder/123` the `folder_id` is `123`. The root folder of a Box account is always represented by the ID `0`.; scope (path) — The scope of the metadata template.; template_key (path) — The name of the metadata template.

GET /2.0/folders/{folder_id}/metadata/{scope}/{template_key}
Retrieves the instance of a metadata template that has been applied to a folder. This can not be used on the root folder with ID `0`.
Required: folder_id (path) — The unique identifier that represent a folder. The ID for any folder can be determined by visiting this folder in the web application and copying the ID from the URL. For example, for the URL `https://*.app.box.com/folder/123` the `folder_id` is `123`. The root folder of a Box account is always represented by the ID `0`.; scope (path) — The scope of the metadata template.; template_key (path) — The name of the metadata template.

GET /2.0/folders/{folder_id}
Gets the information for a shared link on a folder.
Required: folder_id (path) — The unique identifier that represent a folder. The ID for any folder can be determined by visiting this folder in the web application and copying the ID from the URL. For example, for the URL `https://*.app.box.com/folder/123` the `folder_id` is `123`. The root folder of a Box account is always represented by the ID `0`.; fields (query) — Explicitly request the `shared_link` fields to be returned for this item.
